    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "09423969_a4217ee8",
        "filename": "java/droiddoc.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 271,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136354
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-10T20:39:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That seem against current design a little bit. Tor\u0027s design was that Metalava also handles calling the documentation tool(Javadoc/dokka) in a  new process using \"--generate-documentation\" as args separator so that after Metalava generate stubs source for docs, it will tell the documentation tool where the sources it can find.\n\nBasically, we supply \"--generate-documentation arg1 arg2...\" to Metalava, then the next argument is the documentation tool to invoke (e.g. pass in javadoc.path), and all remaining arguments are passed to documentation tool as arguments by Metalava. And then Metalava will call the documentation tool to run.",
      "parentUuid": "1edc19d6_c98187a5",
      "revId": "43dd2688cc72855e80213d26bc7167aff30126b6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7c52bc90_f8f7dc86",
        "filename": "java/droiddoc.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 271,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-10T20:41:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s there to be a drop-in replacment for droiddoc, but in the platform build we can do better.  We don\u0027t want to wait for docs generation just to build android_stubs_current, and we don\u0027t want to have to run metalava twice to build android_stubs_current and the docs.",
      "parentUuid": "09423969_a4217ee8",
